      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: MKR Vidor 4000] [Product category: MKR Family] [Element of MKR Vidor 4000: None] [Tutorial about MKR Vidor 4000: None] \n\n1.1 Microcontroller Block\nThe board's microcontroller is a low power Arm® Cortex®-M0 32-bit SAMD21, like in the other boards within the Arduino MKR family. The Wi-Fi® and Bluetooth® connectivity is performed with a module from u-blox, the NINAW10, a low power chipset operating in the 2.4GHz range. On top of that, secure communication is ensured through the Microchip® ECC508 crypto chip. Also, you can find a battery charger, and a directionable RGB LED on-board.\nMicrocontroller, Details = SAMD21 Arm® Cortex®-M0+ 32bit low power ARM. USB connector, Details = Micro USB (USB-B). Built-in LED Pin, Details = Pin 6. Digital I/O Pins, Details = x8. Analog Input Pins, Details = x7 (ADC 8/10/12 bit). Analog Output Pins, Details = x1 (DAC 10 bit). PMWPins, Details = x13 (0 - 8, 10, 12, A3, A4). External interrupts, Details = x10 (Pin 0, 1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8,9, A1, A2). Bluetooth®, Details = Nina W102 u-blox® module. Wi-Fi®, Details = Nina W102 u-blox® module. Secure element, Details = ATECC508A. UART, Details = Yes. I2C, Details = Yes. SPI, Details = Yes. I/O Voltage, Details = 3.3 V. Input Voltage (nominal), Details = 5-7 V. DC Current per I/O pin, Details = 7 mA. Supported battery Li-Po Single Cell, 3.7 V, 1024 mAh, Details = Minimum. Battery connector, Details = JST PH. Processor, Details = 48 MHz. RTC, Details = 32.768 kHz. SAMD21G18A, Details = 256 kB Flash, 32 kB SRAM. Nina W102 u-blox® module, Details = 448 kB ROM, 520 kB SRAM, 2 MB Flash",
      "product_category": "MKR Family",
      "chunk_id": "MKR Vidor 4000-datasheet::c4"
    },
    {
      "product": "MKR Vidor 4000",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: MKR Vidor 4000] [Product category: MKR Family] [Element of MKR Vidor 4000: None] [Tutorial about MKR Vidor 4000: None] \n\n2.1 Recommended Operating Conditions\nThe following table is a comprehensive guideline for the optimal use of the MKR Vidor 4000, outlining typical operating conditions and design limits. The operating conditions of the MKR Vidor 4000 are largely a function based on its component's specifications.\nUSB Supply Input Voltage, Min = -. USB Supply Input Voltage, Typ = 5.0. USB Supply Input Voltage, Max = -. USB Supply Input Voltage, Unit = V. Battery Supply Input Voltage, Min = -. Battery Supply Input Voltage, Typ = 3.7. Battery Supply Input Voltage, Max = -. Battery Supply Input Voltage, Unit = V. Supply Input Voltage, Min = -. Supply Input Voltage, Typ = 5.0. Supply Input Voltage, Max = 6.0. Supply Input Voltage, Unit = V. Microprocessor Circuit Operating Voltage, Min = -. Microprocessor Circuit Operating Voltage, Typ = 3.3. Microprocessor Circuit Operating Voltage, Max = -. Microprocessor Circuit Operating Voltage, Unit = V. FPGA Circuit Operating Voltage, Min = -. FPGA Circuit Operating Voltage, Typ = 3.3. FPGA Circuit Operating Voltage, Max = -. FPGA Circuit Operating Voltage, Unit = V",
      "product_category": "MKR Family",
      "chunk_id": "MKR Vidor 4000-datasheet::c9"
    },
    {
      "product": "MKR Vidor 4000",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: MKR Vidor 4000] [Product category: MKR Family] [Element of MKR Vidor 4000: None] [Tutorial about MKR Vidor 4000: None] \n\n3.3 Power Supply\nThe MKR Vidor can be powered through one of these interfaces:\n- USB: Micro USB-B port. Used to power the board at 5 V.\n- Vin: This pin can be used to power the board with a regulated 5 V source. If the power is fed through this pin, the USB power source is disconnected. This is the only way you can supply 5 V (range is 5 V to maximum 6 V) to the board not using USB. The pin is only an INPUT.\n- 5V: This pin outputs 5 V from the board when powered from the USB connector or from the VIN pin of the board. It is unregulated and the voltage is taken directly from the inputs.\n- VCC: This pin outputs 3.3 V through the on-board voltage regulator. This voltage is 3.3 V if USB or VIN is used.\n- Battery: 3.7 V single-cell lithium-ion/lithium-polymer battery, connected through the onboard battery connector JST S2B-PH-SM4-TB(LF)(SN). The mating connector is JST PHR-2.",
      "product_category": "MKR Family",
