      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n6.1 Pinout\nThe Arduino® UNO R4 WiFi pinout is shown in the following figure.\nGND, Function = Ground. 3.3 V, Function = 3.3 V Power Rail. 5V, Function = 5V Power Rail. VIN, Function = Voltage Input. SDA, Function = I2C Data. SCL, Function = I2C Clock. A0, Function = Analog Input 0 / DAC. A1, Function = Analog Input 1 / OPAMP+. A2, Function = Analog Input 2 / OPAMP-. A3, Function = Analog Input 3 / OPAMPOut. A4, Function = Analog Input 4 / I2C Serial Data (SDA). A5, Function = Analog Input 5 / I2C Serial Clock (SCL). D0, Function = Digital I/O 0 / UART RX. D1, Function = Digital I/O 1 / UART TX. D2-D13, Function = Digital I/O 2-13. D14 (TXD), Function = Serial Transmit (UART). D15 (RXD), Function = Serial Receive (UART). CANRX, Function = CAN Receiver (requires external transceiver). CANTX, Function = CAN Transmitter (requires external transceiver)\nArduino® UNO R4 WiFi Pinout",
