      "text": "[Product: Alvik] [Product category: Education] [Element of Alvik: None] [Tutorial about Alvik: None] \n\n2.1 Topology\nThe main parts of the robot are the following:\nAlvik's main part from top to bottom (left) and bottom to top (right)\nArduino® Nano ESP32, Quantity = 1. Arduino® Nano ESP32, Details = Main controller of the robot. Main PCB, Quantity = 1. Main PCB, Details = Main PCB of the robot. STM32 Arm® Cortex®-M4 32 Bit, Quantity = 1. STM32 Arm® Cortex®-M4 32 Bit, Details = Onboard STM32 auxiliary controller. Touch Programmable button, Quantity = 7. Touch Programmable button, Details = Touch programmable buttons integrated on the main PCB. ON/OFF Power Switch, Quantity = 1. ON/OFF Power Switch, Details = Assembled on the main PCB. RGB LED, Quantity = 2. RGB LED, Details = Fully programmable RGB LED mounted on the main PCB. Color Sensor, Quantity = 1. Color Sensor, Details = RGB Color detector. 6-Axis Gyro/Accelerometer, Quantity = 1. 6-Axis Gyro/Accelerometer, Details = 6-Axis Gyro and Accelerometer sensor. Front PCB, Quantity = 1. Front PCB, Details = Robot auxiliary PCB with additional sensors. ToF Distance Sensor, Quantity = 1. ToF Distance Sensor, Details = Time-of-Flight Distance sensor up to 350 cm , mounted on the Front PCB. Line follower array, Quantity = 1. Line follower array, Details = Line follower array made up of 3 phototransistors and 4 infrared LEDs, mounted on the front PCB. Grove Connector, Quantity = 2. Grove Connector, Details = I2C Grove Connector to extend robot's capabilities\nQwiic Connector, Quantity = 2. Qwiic Connector, Details = I2C Qwiic Connector to extend robot capabilities. Servomotor Connector, Quantity = 2. Servomotor Connector, Details = 3-pins connector to attach servomotors. 18650 Li-Ion Battery, Quantity = 1. 18650 Li-Ion Battery, Details = Battery of the robot. Main Chassis, Quantity = 1. Main Chassis, Details = Main chassis of the robot made in plastic. Motor holder, Quantity = 2. Motor holder, Details = Plastic support to hold the motor in place, a screwdriver is required to open it. Motors, Quantity = 2. Motors, Details = DC Motor with magnetic relative encoder. Rubber wheel, Quantity = 2. Rubber wheel, Details = Rubber wheel with 34 mmof diameter. Inox steal ball9mm, Quantity = 1. Inox steal ball9mm, Details = Ball that serves as third support for stability. Ball caster holder, Quantity = 1. Ball caster holder, Details = Plastic support to hold the steal ball. INOX M3 x 5 mmScrews, Quantity = 5. INOX M3 x 5 mmScrews, Details = Phillips Screws of the robot. Battery cover, Quantity = 1. Battery cover, Details = Cover to hold the battery, a screwdriver is required to open it",
      "product_category": "Education",
      "chunk_id": "Alvik-datasheet::c10"
    },
    {
      "product": "GIGA Display Shield",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: GIGA Display Shield] [Product category: Mega] [Element of GIGA Display Shield: None] [Tutorial about GIGA Display Shield: None] \n\n9 RGB LED\nA common anode RGB (DL1) is driven by a dedicated IS31FL3197-QFLS2-TR RGB LED Driver IC (U2) which can deliver sufficient current to each LED. The RGB LED Driver is connected via a common I2C connection to the GIGA main board. An included integrated charge pump ensures that the voltage delivered to the LED is sufficient.",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "GIGA Display Shield-datasheet::c12"
    },
    {
      "product": "Alvik",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Alvik] [Product category: Education] [Element of Alvik: None] [Tutorial about Alvik: Tutorial_Alvik] \n\n2 Next, gotothe LEDs folder and drag set [left] LED color to TOON] fae (1\\ anannn daa connecting it to the previous command. 3 You need to upload the code to the robot. Remember to turn ON the robot when you",
      "product_category": "Education",
      "chunk_id": "Tutorial_Alvik_Block-Based Language::c6"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n2.3 Microcontroller\nProduct Name, Description = Arduino® UNO R4 WiFi. Microcontroller, Description = Renesas RA4M1 (R7FA4M1AB3CFM#AA0). Clock Speed, Description = 48 MHz. Power Supply, Description = 6-24 VDC via VIN, 5 VDC via USB-C®. Operating Voltage, Description = 5 V (RA4M1). Memory, Description = 256 kB Flash, 32 kB SRAM, 8 kB EEPROM. Peripherals, Description = Capacitive Touch Sensing Unit (CTSU), USB® 2.0 Full-Speed Module, 14-bit ADC, Up to DAC, Operational Amplifier (OPAMP). Communication, Description = 1x UART, 1x SPI, 1x I2C, 1x CAN (external transceiver required). Wi-Fi®, Description = 802.11 b/g/n (Wi-Fi® 4), up to 150 Mbps. Bluetooth®, Description = Bluetooth® 5. LED Matrix, Description = 12x8 red LEDs, fully programmable. Additional Features, Description = Real-time Clock (RTC), Memory Protection Unit (MPU), DAC, DMA. Certifications, Description = CE/RED, UKCA, FCC, IC, RoHS, REACH, WEEE",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c7"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n8.8 Modulino® Pixels\nThe Modulino® Pixels includes eight LC8822-2020 RGB LEDs and uses the STM32C011F4 chip for digital communication, perfect for creating colorful displays and lighting effects in your projects. All of the Modulino® nodes that use dedicated I2C interface controllers have the footprints to provide the option to mount I2C pullup resistors, but no resistors are mounted.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c52"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n1x10 Header for LC8822-2020 and I2C interface controller\nCO, Function = Clock Out. DO, Function = Data Out. RX1, Function = UART Receive. TX1, Function = UART Transmit. SWDIO, Function = SWD Data. SWCLK, Function = SWD Clock. PF2, Function = NRST\nThe header can be used to add more LC8822-2020 RGB's LED in a daisy chain configuration.\nBuilt-in LEDs open for extension\nIt also has other I2C interface controller IC pins usable for other purposes or for reprogramming it using its SWD interface. These provide a place to mount header pins if desired.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c56"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n8.9 Modulino® Buttons\nThe Modulino® Buttons includes three SPST push buttons and three yellow LEDs, using the STM32C011F4 chip for digital communication. It's ideal for creating interactive input interfaces. All of the Modulino® nodes that use dedicated I2C interface controllers have the footprints to provide the option to mount I2C pullup resistors, but no resistors are mounted.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c58"
    }
  ]
