      "product": "Alvik",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Alvik] [Product category: Education] [Element of Alvik: None] [Tutorial about Alvik: None] \n\n1.5.1 Motors\nAlvik is a differential robot driven by two independent DC motors with magnetic relative encoders:\nAlvik's DC Motor Technical Specs\nThe motors have the following technical specifications:\nOperating Voltage, Information = 6 VDC. No load Current, Information = 70 mA. Max load Current, Information = 90 mA. No load Speed, Information = 96 rpm. Magnetic relative AB encoder, Information = 3 ppr\nThe two motors are driven by the MAX22211 motors driver:\nDual Motor Driver, Part Name = MAX22211. Dual Motor Driver, Product page = Link. Dual Motor Driver, Datasheet = Link",
      "product_category": "Education",
      "chunk_id": "Alvik-datasheet::c7"
    },
    {
      "product": "Make Your UNO Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Make Your UNO Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Make Your UNO Kit: None] [Tutorial about Make Your UNO Kit: None] \n\n2.2 Power Consumption\nVINMax, Description = Maximum input voltage from Jack connector/VIN pad. VINMax, Min = 6. VINMax, Typ = -. VINMax, Max = 20. VINMax, Unit = V. VUSBMax, Description = Maximum input voltage from USB connector. VUSBMax, Min = . VUSBMax, Typ = -. VUSBMax, Max = 5.5. VUSBMax, Unit = V. PMax, Description = Maximum Power Consumption. PMax, Min = -. PMax, Typ = -. PMax, Max = xx. PMax, Unit = mA",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Make Your UNO Kit-datasheet::c8"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n4.1 Recommended Operating Conditions\nV IN, Description = Input voltage from VIN pad / DC Jack. V IN, Min = 6. V IN, Typ = 7.0. V IN, Max = 24. V IN, Unit = V. V USB, Description = Input voltage from USB connector. V USB, Min = 4.8. V USB, Typ = 5.0. V USB, Max = 5.5. V USB, Unit = V. T OP, Description = Operating Temperature. T OP, Min = -40. T OP, Typ = 25. T OP, Max = 85. T OP, Unit = °C\nNote: V DD controls the logic level and is connected to the 5V power rail. V AREF is for the analog logic.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c9"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n6.2.1 Supply Options\nPower for the Arduino® UNO R4 WiFi can be supplied through either the VIN pin or the USB-C® connector.\n- VIN Pin: When power is supplied via the VIN pin, the ISL854102FRZ buck converter reduces the voltage to 5 V. This input is protected by Schottky diodes for reverse polarity and overvoltage protection.\n- USB-C Connector: Power supplied via the USB-C connector provides approximately 4.7 V to the RA4M1 MCU, accounting for the voltage drop due to the Schottky diodes.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c12"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n6.2.2 Power Tree\nThe power distribution system ensures proper voltage levels for all components. The ISL854102 buck converter and SGM2205 regulator manage voltage regulation. Diodes for protection are also represented.\nArduino® UNO R4 WiFi power tree",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c13"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n6.2.3 Pin Specifications\nThe general operating voltage for UNO R4 WiFi is 5 V while the ESP32-S3 module's operating voltage is 3.3 V.\nIt is very important that ESP32-S3's pins (3.3 V) do not come in contact with any of the RA4M1's pins (5 V), as this may damage the circuits. The GPIOs on the R7FA4M1AB3CFM#AA0 microcontroller can safely handle up to 8 mA of current. Never connect devices that draw higher current directly to a GPIO as this may damage the circuit. For powering e.g. servo motors, always use an external power supply.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c14"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n8.1.1 Mechanical Information\n- Board dimensions: 41 mm x 25.36 mm\n- Board thickness: 1.6 mm, tolerance ± 0.2 mm\n- 4 mounting holes, nominal diameter 3.2 mm, tolerance -0 mm, +0.2 mm\n- Hole-to-hole quotes: 16 mm vertical, 32 mm horizontal\n- Green power LED powered by 3V3 net, with 1 kΩ series resistor\n- Power LED nominal current consumption: 1mA ≈ (3.3 V - 2.2 V) / 1 kΩ",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c20"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n8.1.3 I2C Address Reference\nNote: The maximum number of Modulino® nodes that can be connected together using this configuration is dependent on the power source and total consumption of the system plus the total length of the cables used. In our tests the maximum number of Modulino® nodes connected together and powered via the USB Type-C of the microcontroller is approximately 50 nodes.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c24"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n8.3.1 Technical Specifications\nSensor, Details = LSM6DSOXTR. Supply Voltage, Details = Min: 1.71 V, Max: 3.6 V. Power Consumption, Details = Accel: 170 µA, Gyro: 0.55 mA. Range, Details = ±125 dps to ±2000 dps. Accuracy, Details = Accel: ±20 mg, Gyro: ±1 dps. Resolution, Details = Accel: 0.061 mg/LSB to 0.488 mg/LSB, Gyro: 4.375 mdps/LSB to 70 mdps/LSB. Communication, Details = SPI, I2C, MIPI I3CSM",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c28"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n8.5.1 Technical Specifications\nSensor, Details = HS3003. Supply Voltage, Details = Min: 2.3 V, Max: 5.5 V. Power Consumption, Details = 24.4 µA (14-bit resolution, 3.3 V supply). Range, Details = 0% to 100% RH, -40°C to +125°C. Accuracy, Details = Humidity: ±2.8%RH, Temperature: ±0.25°C. Resolution, Details = Humidity: 14-bit, Temperature: 14-bit. Communication, Details = I2C",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c40"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n1x4 Header\nGND, Function = Ground. 3.3 V, Function = Power Supply. SDA, Function = I2C Data. SCL, Function = I2C Clock\nThe above pads are generic to all Modulino® nodes and they are on the same bus as the Qwiic connectors. These provide a place to mount header pins if desired.\nDigital\nAnalog\nMain Part\nI2C\nSPI\nOther SERIAL\nAnalog\nUART/USART\nPWM/Timer\nModulino® Movement Pinout\nModulino Movement SKU code:ABX00101 Pinout Last update:18 Jun, 2024",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c30"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n1x4 Header\nGND, Function = Ground. 3.3 V, Function = Power Supply. SDA, Function = I2C Data. SCL, Function = I2C Clock\nThe above pads are generic to all Modulino® nodes and they are on the same bus as the Qwiic connectors. These provide a place to mount header pins if desired.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c36"
    }
  ]
