      "product": "Due",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Due] [Product category: Mega] [Element of Due: None] [Tutorial about Due: None] \n\n6.5.5 Board's 26-Pin Header Connector\nThe 26-pin header connector on the Arduino Due offers a comprehensive set of interfaces and versatile pins crucial for diverse applications\nThese pins offer a range of functionalities, including digital input/output, serial communication, PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) outputs, and I2C (Inter-Integrated Circuit) communication.",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "Due-datasheet::c34"
    },
    {
      "product": "Mega 2560 Rev3",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Mega 2560 Rev3] [Product category: Mega] [Element of Mega 2560 Rev3: None] [Tutorial about Mega 2560 Rev3: None] \n\nATmega2560 处理器\n- 在 16MHz 的⼯作频率下吞吐量⾼达 16 MIPS\n- 256k 字节（其中 8k 字节⽤于引导加载程序）\n- 4k 字节 EEPROM\n- 8k 字节内部 SRAM\n- 带有独⽴振荡器的实时计数器\n- 四个 8 位 PWM 通道\n- 4 个可编程串⾏ USART\n- 控制器 / 外设 SPI 串⾏接⼝",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "Mega 2560 Rev3-datasheet::c46"
    },
    {
      "product": "Opta Analog Expansion A0602",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Opta Analog Expansion A0602] [Product category: Opta Family] [Element of Opta Analog Expansion A0602: None] [Tutorial about Opta Analog Expansion A0602: None] \n\nDescription\nArduino Opta® Analog Expansions are designed to multiply your Opta® micro PLC capabilities with the addition of 8 channels that can be programmed as inputs or outputs for connecting your analog voltage, current, resistive temperature sensors or actuators in addition to 4x dedicated PWM outputs. Designed in partnership with leading relay manufacturer Finder®, it allows professionals to scale up industrial and building automation projects while taking advantage of the Arduino ecosystem.",
      "product_category": "Opta Family",
      "chunk_id": "Opta Analog Expansion A0602-datasheet::c0"
    },
    {
      "product": "Opta Analog Expansion A0602",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Opta Analog Expansion A0602] [Product category: Opta Family] [Element of Opta Analog Expansion A0602: None] [Tutorial about Opta Analog Expansion A0602: None] \n\n2.3.3 PWM Output Channels\nThe Analog Expansion has four PWM output channels (P1...P4) . They are software configurable and for them to work you must provide the V PWM pin with the desired voltage.\nSource voltage supported, Details = 8...24 VDC. Period, Details = Programmable. Duty-cycle, Details = Programmable (0-100%)",
      "product_category": "Opta Family",
      "chunk_id": "Opta Analog Expansion A0602-datasheet::c13"
    },
    {
      "product": "Opta Analog Expansion A0602",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Opta Analog Expansion A0602] [Product category: Opta Family] [Element of Opta Analog Expansion A0602: None] [Tutorial about Opta Analog Expansion A0602: None] \n\n4.3 Input/Output Channels\nThe Arduino Opta® Analog Expansion features 8 channels that can be configured as inputs or outputs. When the channels are configured as inputs they can be used as digital ones with a 0-24/0-10 V range, or analog being able to measure voltage from 0 to 10 V, measure current from 0 to 25 mA or temperature leveraging the RTD mode.\nThe channels I1 and I2 can be used for connecting 3-Wires RTDs. Every channel can be used also as an output, be aware that using more than two channels as an output simultaneously may overheat the device. This will depend on the ambient temperature and channel load.\nWe have tested setting all eight channels as outputs at 25 °C outputting more than 24 mA at 10 V each during a limited timeframe.\nWarning: In case the user needs a configuration with a deviation from the suggested one, will need to validate the system performance and stability before a deployment into a production environment.\nThe PWM outputs are software configurable and for them to work you must provide the V PWM pin with the desired voltage between 8 and 24 VDC, you can set the period and duty-cycle by software.",
      "product_category": "Opta Family",
      "chunk_id": "Opta Analog Expansion A0602-datasheet::c20"
    },
    {
      "product": "Opta Analog Expansion A0602",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Opta Analog Expansion A0602] [Product category: Opta Family] [Element of Opta Analog Expansion A0602: None] [Tutorial about Opta Analog Expansion A0602: None] \n\n4.1 Product View\nArduino Opta® Analog Expansion\n3a, Feature = Power Supply Terminals 12...24 VDC. 3b, Feature = P1...P4 PWMOutputs. 3c, Feature = Power Status LED. 3d, Feature = Analog Input/Output Terminals I1...I2 (Voltage, Current, RTD 2 wires and RTD 3 wires). 3e, Feature = Status LEDs 1...8. 3f, Feature = Port for communication and connection of auxiliary modules. 3g, Feature = Analog Input/Output Terminals I3...I6 (Voltage, Current, RTD 2 wires). 3h, Feature = Analog Input/Output Terminals O1...O2 (Voltage, Current, RTD 2 wires)",
      "product_category": "Opta Family",
      "chunk_id": "Opta Analog Expansion A0602-datasheet::c18"
    },
    {
      "product": "Portenta Proto Kit VE",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Portenta Proto Kit VE] [Product category: Pro Solutions Kits] [Element of Portenta Proto Kit VE: None] [Tutorial about Portenta Proto Kit VE: None] \n\n2.1.4 Portenta Mid Carrier (SKU: ASX00055)\nThe Portenta Mid Carrier expands connectivity options for Portenta family boards, including Ethernet, USB-A, mPCIe, CAN, MicroSD and 4G. It also features JTAG pins for debugging and supports I2C, SPI, PWM, digital and analog I/Os.\nPortenta Mid Carrier\nBelow is a summary of the most important specifications of the Portenta Mid Carrier:\nCompatible Boards, Specification = Portenta X8, Portenta H7 (except MIPI Camera), Portenta C33 (except MIPI Camera). Camera Interfaces, Specification = MIPI Connector (x1), Arducam Connector (x1), USB-A (x1). Display Interface, Specification = DSI (x1). Communication Interfaces, Specification = 4G (mPCIe, x1), Ethernet (x1), SPI (x2), I2C (x3), UART (x4), CAN FD (x2, one without transceiver), I2S (x1), SAI (x1), PDM (x1), SPDIF (x1). User Interface, Specification = Power On Push Button (x1). Storage, Specification = MicroSD card slot (x1). Hardware Debugging, Specification = JTAG/SWD. Power Supply, Specification = Board operating voltage (VIN): +5 VDC; Maximum current provided: 2 A. Dimensions, Specification = 114 mmx86.5mm\nFor detailed information about the Portenta Mid Carrier, please refer to its corresponding documentation available on Arduino Docs: Portenta Mid Carrier Official Documentation [11]",
      "product_category": "Pro Solutions Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Portenta Proto Kit VE-datasheet::c8"
    },
    {
      "product": "Portenta Proto Kit ME",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Portenta Proto Kit ME] [Product category: Pro Solutions Kits] [Element of Portenta Proto Kit ME: None] [Tutorial about Portenta Proto Kit ME: None] \n\n2.1.3 Portenta Mid Carrier (SKU: ASX00055)\nThe Arduino Portenta Mid Carrier expands connectivity options for Portenta family boards, including Ethernet, USBA, mPCIe, CAN, MicroSD, and 4G. It also features JTAG pins for debugging and supports I2C, SPI, PWM, digital, and analog I/Os.\nPortenta Mid Carrier\nBelow is a summary of the most important specifications of the Portenta Mid Carrier:\nCompatible Boards, Specification = Portenta X8, Portenta H7 (except MIPI Camera), Portenta C33 (except MIPI Camera). Camera Interfaces, Specification = MIPI Connector (x1), Arducam Connector (x1), USB-A (x1). Display Interface, Specification = DSI (x1). Communication Interfaces, Specification = 4G (mPCIe, x1), Ethernet (x1), SPI (x2), I2C (x3), UART (x4), CAN FD (x2, one without transceiver), I2S (x1), SAI (x1), PDM (x1), SPDIF (x1). User Interface, Specification = Power On Push Button (x1). Storage, Specification = MicroSD card slot (x1). Hardware Debugging, Specification = JTAG/SWD. Power Supply, Specification = Board operating voltage (VIN): +5 VDC; Maximum current provided: 2 A. Dimensions, Specification = 114 mmx86.5mm\nFor detailed information about the Portenta Mid Carrier, please refer to its corresponding documentation available on Arduino Docs: Portenta Mid Carrier Official Documentation [10]",
      "product_category": "Pro Solutions Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Portenta Proto Kit ME-datasheet::c7"
    },
    {
      "product": "Edge Control",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Edge Control] [Product category: Pro Solutions Kits] [Element of Edge Control: None] [Tutorial about Edge Control: None] \n\n6.1 J1 LCD Connector\n1, Function = PWM. 1, Type = Power. 1, Description = Backlight LED Cathode (PWM control). 2, Function = Power On. 2, Type = Digital. 2, Description = Button input. 3, Function = +5V LCD. 3, Type = Power. 3, Description = LCD power supply. 4, Function = LCD RS. 4, Type = Digital. 4, Description = LCD RS signal. 5, Function = Contrast. 5, Type = Analog. 5, Description = LCD Contrast control. 6, Function = LCD RW. 6, Type = Digital. 6, Description = LCD Read/Write signal. 7, Function = LED+. 7, Type = Power. 7, Description = Backlight LED Anode. 8, Function = LCD EN. 8, Type = Digital. 8, Description = LCD Enable signal. 10, Function = LCD D4. 10, Type = Digital. 10, Description = LCD D4 signal. 12, Function = LCD D5. 12, Type = Digital. 12, Description = LCD D5 signal. 14, Function = LCD D6. 14, Type = Digital. 14, Description = LCD D6 signal. 16, Function = LCD D7. 16, Type = Digital. 16, Description = LCD D7 signal. 9,11,13,15, Function = GND. 9,11,13,15, Type = Power. 9,11,13,15, Description = Ground",
      "product_category": "Pro Solutions Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Edge Control-datasheet::c28"
    },
    {
      "product": "Portenta Machine Control",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Portenta Machine Control] [Product category: Pro Solutions Kits] [Element of Portenta Machine Control: None] [Tutorial about Portenta Machine Control: None] \n\n4x Analog output channels\n- DC Voltage output software configurable: 0-10V DC\n- Max 20mA per channel\n- Analog Out Channel 2 with maximum period of ~1.3 ms (Recommended for high-frequency PWM signals)\n- Analog Out Channels 0, 1, 3 with standard timers",
      "product_category": "Pro Solutions Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Portenta Machine Control-datasheet::c5"
    },
    {
      "product": "Portenta Machine Control",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Portenta Machine Control] [Product category: Pr Solutions] [Element of Portenta Machine Control: None] [Tutorial about Portenta Machine Control: Tutorial_Portenta Machine Control] \n\nThe High-Resolution Timer (HRTIM) function on PG7 allows for highfrequency PWM signals with precise control over short periods. However, it is limited to a maximum period of approximately 1.3 ms. This constraint makes Analog Out Channel 2 optimal for e high-frequency PWM applications but unsuitable for periods exceeding 1.3 ms. For longer periods, alternative Analog Out channels (AOO, AO1, AO3) with standard timers are recommended. Please refer to the Portenta Machine Control User Manual:\nAnalog Outputs section for more details. Encoders The handling of encoders has been updated in the Arduino_PortentaMachineCont rol Library for a more streamlined and intuitive approach. One key new feature is the removal of array object access. In the previous library version, encoder objects were accessed using array notation ( [] ).",
      "product_category": "Pr Solutions",
      "chunk_id": "Tutorial_Portenta Machine Control_Library Guide::c9"
    },
    {
      "product": "Portenta Machine Control",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Portenta Machine Control] [Product category: Pr Solutions] [Element of Portenta Machine Control: None] [Tutorial about Portenta Machine Control: Tutorial_Portenta Machine Control] \n\nOutput Channel 2 (AQ2) Analog output channel 2 (AOQ2) of the Portenta Machine Control is connected to pin PG7 on the Portenta H7, which features an HRTIM (HighResolution TlMer) function. It is the only Analog Out pin on the Portenta Machine Control with an HRTIM The HRTIM on PG7 is mainly applicable for high-frequency PWM signals, which have constraints on the maximum period that can be achieved.",
      "product_category": "Pr Solutions",
      "chunk_id": "Tutorial_Portenta Machine Control_User Manual::c30"
    }
  ]
