    {
      "product": "DIN Simul8",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: DIN Simul8] [Product category: Education] [Element of DIN Simul8: None] [Tutorial about DIN Simul8: None] \n\nDescription\nArduino® DIN Simul8 is a digital-input-simulator and power distribution board for the Arduino Opta® family and Arduino® PLC Starter Kit. It provides eight toggle switches (0 - 10 V output) and four screw terminal for bringing the 24 V and the GROUND easily to the PLC or other board.",
      "product_category": "Education",
      "chunk_id": "DIN Simul8-datasheet::c0"
    },
    {
      "product": "Opta",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Opta] [Product category: Opta Family] [Element of Opta: None] [Tutorial about Opta: None] \n\nDescription\nArduino Opta® is a secure, easy-to-use micro PLC with Industrial IoT capabilities. Designed in partnership with leading relay manufacturer Finder®, it allows professionals to scale up industrial and building automation projects while taking advantage of the Arduino ecosystem.\nThe Arduino Opta® family has three variants: the Arduino Opta® Lite, Arduino Opta® RS485, and Arduino Opta® WiFi, all of them documented inside this document.",
      "product_category": "Opta Family",
      "chunk_id": "Opta-datasheet::c0"
    },
    {
      "product": "Opta",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Opta] [Product category: Opta Family] [Element of Opta: None] [Tutorial about Opta: None] \n\n1 Product Variants\nThere are three variants of the Arduino Opta® created to fit the different needs of each industry and application. The difference between each of the variants can be found in the following table:\nSKU, Arduino Opta® Lite = AFX00003. SKU, Arduino Opta® RS485 = AFX00001. SKU, Arduino Opta® WiFi = AFX00002. USB, Arduino Opta® Lite = USB-C®. USB, Arduino Opta® RS485 = USB-C®. USB, Arduino Opta® WiFi = USB-C®. Ethernet Support, Arduino Opta® Lite = 10/100BASE-T Port. Ethernet Support, Arduino Opta® RS485 = 10/100BASE-T Port. Ethernet Support, Arduino Opta® WiFi = 10/100BASE-T Port. RS-485, Arduino Opta® Lite = N/A. RS-485, Arduino Opta® RS485 = Half-duplex. RS-485, Arduino Opta® WiFi = Half-duplex. Wi-Fi®, Arduino Opta® Lite = N/A. Wi-Fi®, Arduino Opta® RS485 = N/A. Wi-Fi®, Arduino Opta® WiFi = 802.11 b/g/n. Bluetooth®, Arduino Opta® Lite = N/A. Bluetooth®, Arduino Opta® RS485 = N/A. Bluetooth®, Arduino Opta® WiFi = Bluetooth® Low Energy",
      "product_category": "Opta Family",
      "chunk_id": "Opta-datasheet::c3"
    },
    {
      "product": "Opta",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Opta] [Product category: Opta Family] [Element of Opta: None] [Tutorial about Opta: None] \n\n2 Application Examples\nArduino Opta® is designed for industrial standard machinery control as a PLC with advanced features such as AI and connectivity capabilities. It is readily integrated into the Arduino hardware and software ecosystem, including real-time monitoring via the Arduino Cloud.\n- Conveyor belt management: Arduino Opta® offers the possibility to configure its inputs as digital or analog to flexibly collect data from several types of sensors. Thanks to the Wi-Fi®/Bluetooth® Low Energy connectivity, Arduino Opta® can also be smoothly integrated with sensing boards, like the Nicla® ones from the Arduino ecosystem, leveraging Arduino Opta's potential with vision, sound, weight detection, air quality measurement and many other capabilities.\nArduino Opta® can use the data from the various sensors as they are or, thanks to its powerful microcontroller, use the outcome from a computation, to operate a wide variety of industrial machinery through its highperforming relays.\nAll these features, wrapped in a compact form factor, make Arduino Opta® the ideal solution for product flow management in conveyor belts, automated packing or bottling lines.\n- Real-time industrial monitoring: Get instant access to your factory floor data and to the insights of your industrial processes to leverage your manufacturing excellence to continuous improvement. Implement visual management and KPIs monitoring thanks to the Arduino Opta's built-in connectivity features (Ethernet on all the product variants, Fieldbus and WiFi®/Bluetooth® Low Energy upon choice), delivering in a simple, fast and reliable way the data collected through beautiful dashboards in Arduino Cloud.\n- Predictive maintenance: Combine the possibility to interact with wireless and wired sensors, given by the multiple connectivity options of Arduino Opta®, with the powerful microcontroller computational capabilities to implement AI algorithms for predictive maintenance. Edge computing and monitoring capabilities, thanks to the Arduino Cloud features, can help to identify small drifts in your processes to address issues before they become a problem, reducing production line downtimes and ensuring quality outcomes.",
      "product_category": "Opta Family",
      "chunk_id": "Opta-datasheet::c4"
    },
    {
      "product": "Opta",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Opta] [Product category: Opta Family] [Element of Opta: None] [Tutorial about Opta: None] \n\n3.1 General Specifications Overview\nSupply Voltage, Details = 12...24 VDC. Inputs, Details = 8x Analog/Digital inputs. Outputs, Details = 4x Relays - Normally Open (NO) - Max: 10 A each. Processor, Details = Dual-core ST STM32H747XI Processor. Program Memory, Details = 1 MB of RAM. Flash Memory, Details = 2 MB. Flash QSPI Interface, Details = 16 MB Flash QSPI. Shared between manufacturer's internal usage and data logging. Programming method, Details = Arduino + IEC-61131-3 (LD - SFC - FBD - ST - IL). USB Connectivity, Details = Host and Device operation, Programming/Flashing, Power delivery for programming (Not intended to drive external high-power peripherals). Communication, Details = Ethernet, RS-485 (AFX00001 & AFX00002), Wi-Fi® 2.4 GHz and Bluetooth® LE 4.2 supported by firmware, 5.1 supported by hardware (AFX00002). RTC, Details = ~10 days, NTP sync through Wi-Fi® (AFX00002 only) or Ethernet. Security, Details = ATECC608B Crypto Microchip®. Degree of Protection, Details = IP20. Certifications, Details = cULus, ENEC, FCC, CE, CB, UKCA",
      "product_category": "Opta Family",
      "chunk_id": "Opta-datasheet::c5"
    },
    {
      "product": "Opta",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Opta] [Product category: Opta Family] [Element of Opta: None] [Tutorial about Opta: None] \n\n3.2 Processor\nST STM32H747XI Processor, Details = Dual-core. ST STM32H747XI Processor, Details = Arm® Cortex®-M7 core at up to 480 MHz + Arm® 32-bit Cortex®-M4 core at up to 240 MHz. ST STM32H747XI Processor, Details = Flash Memory. ST STM32H747XI Processor, Details = 2 MB of Flash Memory with read-while-write support. ST STM32H747XI Processor, Details = Programming Memory. ST STM32H747XI Processor, Details = 1 MB of RAM",
      "product_category": "Opta Family",
