      "product": "Nicla Vision",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Nicla Vision] [Product category: Nicla Family] [Element of Nicla Vision: None] [Tutorial about Nicla Vision: Tutorial_Nicla Vision] \n\n—— Click on the \"Play\" button at the bottom of the left toolbar. Place some objects on your desk and check if the Nicla Vision can detect them. The MicroPython script does not get compiled and linked into an actual firmware. e Instead it gets copied to the internal Flash of the board where it gets interpreted and executed on the fly. Conclusion In this tritarial voit laarned haw ta MicroPython scripts that then run on the Nicla Vision. You also learned how to configure the camera of the Nicla Vision to be used for machine vision applications in OpenMV. Last but not least you learned how to interact with the built-in LEDs in MicroPython on the OpenMV firmware. Next Steps Familiarize yourself with the OpenMV IDE. There are many other features that did not get mentioned in this tutorial (e.g. the Serial Terminal). Try out other machine vision examples",
      "product_category": "Nicla Family",
      "chunk_id": "Tutorial_Nicla Vision_Blob Detection with OpenMV::c15"
    },
    {
      "product": "Nicla Vision",
