      "product": "Make Your UNO Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Make Your UNO Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Make Your UNO Kit: None] [Tutorial about Make Your UNO Kit: None] \n\n1.1 Application Examples\nThe Make Your UNO Kit is like any UNO board but created by yourself. The UNO board is the flagship product of Arduino.\nRegardless if you are new to the world of electronics or will use the UNO as a tool for education purposes or industry-related tasks.\nFirst entry to electronics: If this is your first project within coding and electronics, get started with our most used and documented board UNO and create one by yourself using the Make Your UNO Kit is a great choice. It is equipped with the well-known ATmega328P processor, 14 digital input/output pins, 6 analog inputs, USB connections, ICSP header and a reset button. This board includes everything you will need for a great first experience with Arduino.\nEducation purposes: Although the UNO board has been with us for about ten years, it is still widely used for various educational purposes and scientific projects. The Make Your UNO Kit is the perfect way to teach and learn about basic circuits, electronics components, soldering and coding microcontrollers, being the perfect board to create basic and advanced projects of all kinds.\nAudio synthesizer for educational and artistic performances : The kit comes with an Audio Synth Shield that can be attached to the Make Your UNO Kit to learn about and experiment with audio synthesizers, being a perfect device to play and experiment in the classroom and at the same time a great instrument for artistic performances.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Make Your UNO Kit-datasheet::c4"
    },
    {
      "product": "Due",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Due] [Product category: Mega] [Element of Due: None] [Tutorial about Due: None] \n\nDescription\nThe Arduino Due is a groundbreaking microcontroller board featuring the Atmel SAM3X8E ARM Cortex-M3 CPU, making it the first Arduino board built around a 32-bit ARM core microcontroller. With its 54x digital input/output pins, 12x analog inputs, 4x UARTs, USB OTG capability, and 84 MHz clock, the Due offers enhanced performance and versatility for a wide range of projects. Compatible with all Arduino shields designed for operation at 3.3 V and compliant with the 1.0 Arduino pinout standard, the Due is a powerful tool for both beginners and experienced makers alike.",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "Due-datasheet::c0"
    },
    {
      "product": "Due",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Due] [Product category: Mega] [Element of Due: None] [Tutorial about Due: None] \n\n2.1 General Specifications Overview\nThe Arduino Due is a versatile microcontroller board designed for a wide range of applications. Powered by the Atmel SAM3X8E ARM Cortex-M3 CPU, it offers high performance and a robust set of features, making it suitable for complex projects. The Due's 32-bit architecture provides enhanced processing capabilities compared to traditional Arduino boards. Designed with a similar form factor to the Arduino® Mega, it maintains compatibility with most Arduino shields through its extensive set of I/O pins and headers. The following table summarizes the board's main features.\nMicrocontroller, Description = Atmel SAM3X8E ARM Cortex-M3 32-bit ARM Cortex-M3 / 84 MHz Clock speed. Memory, Description = SAM3X 512 KB Flash / 96 KB SRAM (divided into two banks: 64 KB and 32 KB). USB-to-serial, Description = ATmega16U2 connected to the SAM3X hardware UART. Digital Inputs, Description = Digital Inputs not 5 V compatible (x54). Analog Inputs, Description = The Due's analog inputs pins measure from ground to a maximum value of 3.3 V (x12). PWMPins, Description = PWMPins with 8 bits resolution (x12). Communication, Description = UART (x4), I2C (x2), SPI (x1 SPI header), Native USB port (x1), Programming USB port (x1). Power, Description = Input voltage (VIN): 7-12 VDC / DC Current per I/O Pin: 8 mA. Dimensions, Description = 101.6 mmx53.34mm. Weight, Description = 36 g. Operating Temperature, Description = -40 °C to +85 °C. Certifications, Description = CE/RED, UKCA, FCC, IC, RCM, RoHS, REACH, WEEE",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "Due-datasheet::c10"
    },
    {
      "product": "Due",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Due] [Product category: Mega] [Element of Due: None] [Tutorial about Due: None] \n\nThe board provides an SPI interface and full access to its pinout as it can be seen in the following table.\nSPI pinout\n1, Function = CIPO. 1, Type = Internal. 1, Description = Controller In Peripheral Out. 2, Function = +5V. 2, Type = Internal. 2, Description = Power Supply of 5V. 3, Function = SCK. 3, Type = Internal. 3, Description = Serial Clock. 4, Function = COPI. 4, Type = Internal. 4, Description = Controller Out Peripheral In. 5, Function = RESET. 5, Type = Internal. 5, Description = Reset. 6, Function = GND. 6, Type = Internal. 6, Description = Ground",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "Due-datasheet::c23"
    },
    {
      "product": "Due",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Due] [Product category: Mega] [Element of Due: None] [Tutorial about Due: None] \n\n6.5.5 Board's 26-Pin Header Connector\nThe 26-pin header connector on the Arduino Due offers a comprehensive set of interfaces and versatile pins crucial for diverse applications\nThese pins offer a range of functionalities, including digital input/output, serial communication, PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) outputs, and I2C (Inter-Integrated Circuit) communication.",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "Due-datasheet::c34"
    },
    {
      "product": "Due",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Due] [Product category: Mega] [Element of Due: None] [Tutorial about Due: None] \n\n描述\nArduino Due 是⼀款开创性的微控制器板，采⽤ Atmel SAM3X8E ARM Cortex-M3 CPU ，是⾸款围绕 32 位 ARM 内核微 控制器构建的 Arduino 板。 Due 具有 54 个数字输⼊ / 输出引脚、 12 个模拟输⼊、 4 个 UART 、 USB OTG 功能和 84 MHz 时钟，可为各种项⽬提供更强的性能和多功能性。 Due 兼容所有⼯作电压为 3.3 V 的 Arduino 扩展板，并符合 1.0 Arduino 引脚布局标准，是初学者和经验丰富的创客们的强⼤⼯具。",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "Due-datasheet::c57"
    },
    {
      "product": "Mega 2560 Rev3",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Mega 2560 Rev3] [Product category: Mega] [Element of Mega 2560 Rev3: None] [Tutorial about Mega 2560 Rev3: None] \n\nDescription\nArduino® Mega 2560 Rev3 is an exemplary development board dedicated for building extensive applications as compared to other maker boards by Arduino. The board accommodates the ATmega2560 microcontroller, which operates at a frequency of 16 MHz. The board contains 54 digital input/output pins, 16 analog inputs, 4 UARTs (hardware serial ports), a USB connection, a power jack, an ICSP header, and a reset button.",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "Mega 2560 Rev3-datasheet::c0"
    },
    {
      "product": "Mega 2560 Rev3",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Mega 2560 Rev3] [Product category: Mega] [Element of Mega 2560 Rev3: None] [Tutorial about Mega 2560 Rev3: None] \n\n描述\n与 Arduino 的其他开发板相⽐， Arduino® Mega 2560 Rev3 是⼀款⽤于构建⼴泛应⽤的⽰范性开发板。该电路板内置 ATmega2560 微控制器，⼯作频率为 16 MHz 。电路板包含 54 个数字输⼊ / 输出引脚、 16 个模拟输⼊、 4 个 UART （硬件 串⾏端⼝） 、⼀个 USB 连接、⼀个电源插孔、⼀个 ICSP 接头和⼀个复位按钮。",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "Mega 2560 Rev3-datasheet::c44"
    },
    {
      "product": "Mega 2560 Rev3",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Mega 2560 Rev3] [Product category: Mega] [Element of Mega 2560 Rev3: None] [Tutorial about Mega 2560 Rev3: None] \n\n1 The Board\nMega 2560 Rev3 is a successor board of Arduino Mega, it is dedicated to applications and projects that require large number of input output pins and the use cases which need high processing power. The Mega 2560 Rev3 comes with a much larger set of IOs when we compare it with the traditional Arduino® UNO board considering the form factor of both the boards.",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "Mega 2560 Rev3-datasheet::c14"
    },
    {
      "product": "Nano",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Nano] [Product category: Nano Family] [Element of Nano: None] [Tutorial about Nano: None] \n\n1.1 Application Examples\nArduino Nano is the first embedded microcontroller in the Nano series with minimum functionalities, designed for mini projects from the maker community. With a large number of input/output pins gives the advantage of utilizing several serial communications like UART, SPI and I2C. The hardware is compatible with Arduino IDE, Arduino CLI and Cloud Editor.\nSecurity : The high-performance and low-power capabilities gives the chance to develop security based applications like access control systems using fingerprint sensors. The flexibility to interface sensors and external devices using serial communication has improved the scope of utility.\nEnvironmental : The low-power feature of the microcontroller and the power supply options for the board has enhanced the ability to implement remote IoT projects related to environmental issues.\nRobotics : Robotics has always been the favorite area of exploration for the Maker community and with this tiny embedded hardware you can now create complex and advanced robotic applications.",
      "product_category": "Nano Family",
      "chunk_id": "Nano-datasheet::c11"
    },
    {
      "product": "Mega 2560 Rev3",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Mega 2560 Rev3] [Product category: Mega] [Element of Mega 2560 Rev3: None] [Tutorial about Mega 2560 Rev3: None] \n\n- 机器⼈： Mega 2560 Rev3 具有⾼处理能⼒，可以处理⼤量机器⼈应⽤。它与电机控制器扩展板兼容，能够同时控制 多个电机，因此⾮常适合机器⼈应⽤。其⼤量的 I/O 引脚也能容纳许多机器⼈传感器。\n- 3D 打印： 算法在 3D 打印机的实施过程中发挥着重要作⽤。 Mega 2560 Rev3 能够处理 3D 打印所需的复杂算法。此 外，使⽤ Arduino IDE 可以轻松地对代码进⾏细微修改，因此可以根据⽤⼾要求定制 3D 打印程序。\n- Wi-Fi ： 该电路板集成⽆线功能，增强了应⽤的实⽤性。 Mega 2560 Rev3 与 Wi-Fi® 扩展板兼容，因此可以为 3D 打 印和机器⼈应⽤提供⽆线功能。",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "Mega 2560 Rev3-datasheet::c52"
    },
    {
      "product": "GIGA R1 WiFi",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: GIGA R1 WiFi] [Product category: Mega] [Element of GIGA R1 WiFi: None] [Tutorial about GIGA R1 WiFi: None] \n\nDescription\nThe Arduino® GIGA R1 WiFi brings the power of the STM32H7 to the Mega form factor, being the first Mega board to include onboard Wi-Fi® and Bluetooth® connectivity. The board provides 76 digital inputs/outputs (13 with PWM capability), 14 analog inputs and 2 analog outputs (DAC) all easily accessible via pin headers. The STM32 microprocessor with dual-core Arm® Cortex®-M7 and Arm® Cortex®-M4, together with onboard memory and audio jack enables you to perform machine learning and signal processing on the edge.",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "GIGA R1 WiFi-datasheet::c0"
    }
  ]
