      "product": "DIN Simul8",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: DIN Simul8] [Product category: Education] [Element of DIN Simul8: None] [Tutorial about DIN Simul8: None] \n\nFeatures\nNote : This board needs the Arduino Opta® for full functionality.\n- Toggle Switches\n- 8 toggle switch in the middle of the board\n- LEDs\n- 8 leds showing the status of each toggle switches\n- Screw connectors\n- 2 screw connectors exposing +24 V DC\n- 2 screw connectors exposing GND\n- 8 screw connectors link to the toggle switches output (0 - 10 V)\n- 1 barrel plug (+24 V DC)\n- DIN mounting\n- RT-072 DIN Rail Modular PCB Board Holders - 72 mm",
      "product_category": "Education",
      "chunk_id": "DIN Simul8-datasheet::c2"
    },
    {
      "product": "Opta Digital Expansion D1608E - D1608S",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Opta Digital Expansion D1608E - D1608S] [Product category: Opta Family] [Element of Opta Digital Expansion D1608E - D1608S: None] [Tutorial about Opta Digital Expansion D1608E - D1608S: None] \n\n3.4 Outputs (AFX00006 Only)\nNumber of outputs, Details = 8x Solid State Relays (NO - SPST). Max current per relay, Details = 3 A. Max peak current per relay, Details = 50 A (10 ms). Continuous current per terminal, Details = 3 A. Short-circuit protection, Details = No, external fuse required. Relay rated voltage, Details = 24 VDC. Switching voltage range, Details = 1.5...30 VDC. Maximum blocking voltage, Details = 33 VDC. Rated load DC13, Details = 36W. Minimum switching current, Details = 1 mA. Max \"OFF-state\" leakage current, Details = 0.001 mA. Max \"ON-state\" voltage drop, Details = 0.4 V. Relay response time from state 0 to state 1, Details = 0.02 ms for relay output. Relay response time from state 1 to state 0, Details = 0.2 ms for relay output. Electrical life at rated load, Details = > 10 million cycles",
      "product_category": "Opta Family",
      "chunk_id": "Opta Digital Expansion D1608E - D1608S-datasheet::c10"
    },
    {
      "product": "Portenta Machine Control",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Portenta Machine Control] [Product category: Pro Solutions Kits] [Element of Portenta Machine Control: None] [Tutorial about Portenta Machine Control: None] \n\n3.4 Digital Outputs\nThe Portenta Machine Control has the following outputs specifications:\n- 8x high side switches (2x TPS4H160AQPWPRQ1 ), one for each channel.\n- The current limit nominal value is 0.6A per channel. Due to internal TPS4H160AQPWPRQ1 circuit tolerances, the real value can be higher, up to 0.9A.\nThe digital output connector (J6) has a 24V IN pin which must be supplied with 24V DC. The 24V IN pin is not galvanically isolated: the input voltage must be referred to the same GND of the board.\nThe supply voltage can be the same 24V which is powering the board.",
      "product_category": "Pro Solutions Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Portenta Machine Control-datasheet::c19"
    },
    {
      "product": "Portenta Machine Control",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Portenta Machine Control] [Product category: Pro Solutions Kits] [Element of Portenta Machine Control: None] [Tutorial about Portenta Machine Control: None] \n\n3.5 Programmable Digital I/O\nThe programmable digital I/O connector has a 24V IN pin which must be supplied with 24V DC.\nThe 24V IN pin is not galvanically isolated: the input voltage must be referred to the same GND of the board.\nThe supply voltage can be the same 24V which is powering the board. There are 3x TPS4H160AQPWPRQ1 chipsets, one for each channel, having a total of 12x high-side switches.",
      "product_category": "Pro Solutions Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Portenta Machine Control-datasheet::c20"
    },
    {
      "product": "Portenta Machine Control",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Portenta Machine Control] [Product category: Pr Solutions] [Element of Portenta Machine Control: None] [Tutorial about Portenta Machine Control: Tutorial_Portenta Machine Control] \n\n+24 VDC, with reverse polarity protection, ensuring the controller remains safeguarded from power irregularities. Digital and analog ports: Equipped with a versatile set of input and output ports, the Portenta Machine Control supports: 8x digital input ports with 8x Status LEDs labeled as DIGITAL INPUTS 8x digital output ports with 8x Status LEDs labeled as DIGITAL OUTPUTS 3x software-configurable analog input ports labeled as ANALOG IN 4x analog output ports labeled as ANALOG OUT 12x digital programmable input/output ports labeled as PROGRAMMABLE DIGITAL I/0 Temperature sensing: With three software-configurable temperature channalce tha Dartanta Machina Control can measure a variety of temperature ranges using: Type K thermocouples Type J thermocouples PT100 sensors Communication interfaces and protocols: Seamless connectivity is a hallmark of this controller.",
      "product_category": "Pr Solutions",
      "chunk_id": "Tutorial_Portenta Machine Control_User Manual::c7"
