    {
      "product": "Modulino Movement",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Modulino Movement] [Product category: Modulino Family] [Element of Modulino Movement: None] [Tutorial about Modulino Movement: None] \n\n1 Application Examples\nBelow are some project ideas focused on the Modulino® Movement module and its built-in LSM6DSOXTR sensor:\n- Gesture Recognition: Harness the 6-axis motion data (accelerometer + gyroscope) to detect custom gestures. You can create interactive controls for games, user interfaces, or home automation-triggering actions when certain patterns (e.g., wrist flicks or device shakes) are recognized.\n- Step Counter or Pedometer: Use the accelerometer data to count steps accurately in wearable or fitnessrelated projects. Log daily movements or design health-oriented applications that notify users of their activity progress.\n- Vibration Monitoring: Monitor vibrations in appliances, machinery, or vehicles using the sensor's highsensitivity accelerometer. Detect anomalies, implement predictive maintenance strategies, or create alert systems for sudden impact or shock events.\n- Orientation and Tilt Control: Measure real-time orientation in space. Ideal for creating tilt-based controls in interactive art installations, DIY game controllers, or robotics projects that respond to angular displacement.\n- IMU-based Stabilization: Leverage both gyroscope and accelerometer data for advanced applications like robotics or drones, where real-time inertial measurements are used to maintain stability and smooth motion control.",
      "product_category": "Modulino Family",
      "chunk_id": "Modulino Movement-datasheet::c3"
    },
    {
      "product": "Modulino Movement",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Modulino Movement] [Product category: Modulino Family] [Element of Modulino Movement: None] [Tutorial about Modulino Movement: None] \n\n4.1 Recommended Operating Conditions\n-Sensor supply range: 1.71 V - 3.6 V -Powered at 3.3 V through the Qwiic interface (in accordance with the Qwiic standard) -Operating temperature: -40 °C to +85 °C\nTypical current consumption:\nAccelerometer: ~170 µA Gyroscope: ~0.55 mA",
      "product_category": "Modulino Family",
      "chunk_id": "Modulino Movement-datasheet::c7"
    },
    {
      "product": "Modulino Movement",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Modulino Movement] [Product category: Modulino Family] [Element of Modulino Movement: None] [Tutorial about Modulino Movement: None] \n\n7 Functional Overview\nThe Modulino® Movement node uses the LSM6DSOXTR sensor for 3 -axis acceleration and 3 -axis gyroscopic measurements. It can detect motion, orientation. Data is accessed through I2C (via the Qwiic connector at 3.3 V) or SPI (through the additional header).",
      "product_category": "Modulino Family",
      "chunk_id": "Modulino Movement-datasheet::c10"
    },
