      "product": "Alvik",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Alvik] [Product category: Education] [Element of Alvik: None] [Tutorial about Alvik: None] \n\n1.1 General Specifications Overview\nAlvik is an educational robot that is battery-powered and has multiple sensors and actuators, like color detection, distance, line following, accelerometer, gyroscope and much more.\nAlvik's Main Components\nAlvik on-board Core, Description = STM32 Arm® Cortex®-M4 32 Bit. Alvik Main Controller, Description = Arduino® Nano ESP32. Connectivity, Description = Wi-Fi®, Bluetooth® LE. Sensors, Description = RGB Color detection, Distance ToF 8x8 Array - up to 350 cm, IMU - 6 degree, 3x Line follower, 7x Touch sensor. Motors, Description = High precision with hall effect encoder. Up to 13 cm/s. Extensions, Description = Servo motor, I2C Grove, Qwiic, Lego® Technic™, M3x5 mmScrews",
      "product_category": "Education",
      "chunk_id": "Alvik-datasheet::c3"
    },
    {
      "product": "Alvik",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Alvik] [Product category: Education] [Element of Alvik: None] [Tutorial about Alvik: None] \n\n1.4 Sensors\nAlvik comes with a large number of onboard sensors, from color detection to distance sensors or inertial measurement units, all of which are listed in the following table:\nColor detection (x1), Part Name = APDS 9660. Color detection (x1), Product page = Link. Color detection (x1), Datasheet = Link. IMU (x1), Part Name = LSM6DSOX. IMU (x1), Product page = Link. IMU (x1), Datasheet = Link. Time of Flight distance sensor (x1), Part Name = VL53L7CXV0GC. Time of Flight distance sensor (x1), Product page = Link. Time of Flight distance sensor (x1), Datasheet = Link. Line Follower Array (x3), Part Name = Custom made. Line Follower Array (x3), Product page = -. Line Follower Array (x3), Datasheet = -. Capacitive Touch buttons (x7), Part Name = Custom made. Capacitive Touch buttons (x7), Product page = -. Capacitive Touch buttons (x7), Datasheet = -\nThe sensory capabilities of Alvik can be expanded using the different connectors and communication protocols available at the back of the robot.",
      "product_category": "Education",
      "chunk_id": "Alvik-datasheet::c5"
    },
    {
      "product": "Alvik",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Alvik] [Product category: Education] [Element of Alvik: None] [Tutorial about Alvik: None] \n\n2.4 Robot Expandability\nAlvik is a robot designed to be used in STEAM & Maker environments where openness and wide compatibility with other products and construction systems are key. Thanks to that Alvik's capabilities can be expanded with new sensors and actuators using the additional connectors on its back, and with additional mechanical extensions like Lego® Technic™ pieces or 3D printed/custom made parts. In the following sections we will explain how to expand Alvik's capabilities.",
      "product_category": "Education",
      "chunk_id": "Alvik-datasheet::c15"
    },
    {
      "product": "Braccio Carrier",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Braccio Carrier] [Product category: Education] [Element of Braccio Carrier: None] [Tutorial about Braccio Carrier: None] \n\n5.3 Online Resources\nNow that you have gone through the basics of what you can do with the board you can explore the endless possibilities it provides by checking exciting projects on Project Hub [2] , the Arduino Library Reference [3] and the online store [4] where you will be able to complement your board with sensors, actuators and more.",
      "product_category": "Education",
      "chunk_id": "Braccio Carrier-datasheet::c22"
    },
    {
      "product": "Alvik",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Alvik] [Product category: Education] [Element of Alvik: None] [Tutorial about Alvik: None] \n\n1 Features\n1.1 General Specifications Overview, 1 = 4. 1.2 Related Accessories (Included), 1 = 5. 1.3 Controllers, 1 = 5. 1.4 Sensors, 1 = 5. 1.5 Actuators, 1 = 5. 1.5.1 Motors, 1 = 6. 1.5.2 RGB LEDs, 1 = 7. 1.6 Connectors & Communication Protocols, 1 = 7. 2 Functional Overview, 1 = 8. 2.1 Topology, 1 = 8. 2.2 Block Diagram, 1 = 10. 2.3 Power Supply, 1 = 11. 2.3.1 Robot's Battery, 1 = 12. 2.3.2 ON/OFF Power Switch, 1 = 13. 2.4 Robot Expandability, 1 = 14. 2.4.1 Additional Connectors, 1 = 14. 2.4.2 Lego® Technic™ Compatibility, 1 = 15. 2.4.3 M3 Screw Inserters Compatibility, 1 = 16. 3 Device Operation, 1 = 17. 3.1 Getting Started - MicroPython, 1 = 17. 3.2 Getting Started - Arduino IDE, 1 = 17. 3.3 Getting Started - Arduino Cloud, 1 = 17. 3.4 Sample Sketches, 1 = 17. 3.5 Online Resources, 1 = 17. 4 Product Compliance, 1 = 18. 4.1 Certifications Summary, 1 = 18. 4.2 Declaration of Conformity CE DoC (EU), 1 = 18. 4.3 Declaration of Conformity to EU RoHS & REACH 211 01/19/2021, 1 = 18. 4.4 Conflict Minerals Declaration, 1 = 19. 4.5 FCC Caution, 1 = 19. 5 Laser Safety Information, 1 = 20. 6 Company Information, 1 = 21\n7 Reference Documentation, 1 = 21. 8 Revision History, 1 = 21",
      "product_category": "Education",
