    {
      "product": "Alvik",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Alvik] [Product category: Education] [Element of Alvik: None] [Tutorial about Alvik: Tutorial_Alvik] \n\n< Go Back Hardware Alvik Vv Tutorials Arduino Alvik API Overview Getting Started with Alvik Start With Alvik And Block-Based Language Setting up Alvik on Arduino IDE Alvik User Manual Search on Docs Home / Hardware / Alvik / Start With Alvik And Block-Based Language Start With Alvik And Block-Based Language Take your first steps with Arduino® Alvik and mBlock. Gaia Last Castronovo revision » 01/20/2025 Alvik Robot Welcome to your first steps with Alvik, your companion for exploring robotics and programming. In this guide, we'll walk you through setting up your Alvik and starting your journey with block based language. What's Included in the Box When unboxing Alvik, you should find the following items:\nAlvik robot USB-C® cable (located under the cardboard tray) Alvik's battery is protected by a pull-tab protective sticker. Remove the sticker to start working with the robot.",
      "product_category": "Education",
      "chunk_id": "Tutorial_Alvik_Block-Based Language::c0"
    },
    {
      "product": "Make Your UNO Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Make Your UNO Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Make Your UNO Kit: None] [Tutorial about Make Your UNO Kit: None] \n\n3.4.2 Getting Started - IDE\nIf you want to program your UNO while offline you need to install the Arduino Desktop IDE [1]. To connect the UNO to your computer, you'll need a USB-C® cable. This also provides power to the board, as indicated by the LED.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Make Your UNO Kit-datasheet::c13"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n2.2 Accessories\nUSB-C® cable, Included = Yes. USB-C® cable, Quantity = 1. I2C Qwiic cables, Included = Yes. I2C Qwiic cables, Quantity = 7. M3x10 screws, Included = Yes. M3x10 screws, Quantity = 24. M3 bolts, Included = Yes. M3 bolts, Quantity = 20. M3x20 female spacers, Included = Yes. M3x20 female spacers, Quantity = 4",
