    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n9.1 Getting Started - IDE\nIf you want to program your Arduino® Plug and Make Kit while offline you need to install the Arduino® Desktop IDE [1] . To connect the Arduino® UNO R4 WiFi to your computer, you will need a USB-C® cable, which can also provide power to the board, as indicated by the LED (DL1).",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c63"
    },
    {
      "product": "Alvik",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Alvik] [Product category: Education] [Element of Alvik: None] [Tutorial about Alvik: Tutorial_Alvik] \n\nis the name of the USB port that your computer assigned to the Nano ESP32. There are several ways to find it, depending on your Operating System, for example:\nYou can use the Arduino IDE to know the port by following this guide. You can look it using the Arduino Lab for MicroPython by clicking Connect after have connected the Alvik with the USB cable. You can look at the list of the USB devices attached to the PC 1 Test Hello World!",
      "product_category": "Education",
      "chunk_id": "Tutorial_Alvik_User Manual::c11"
    },
    {
      "product": "Due",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Due] [Product category: Mega] [Element of Due: None] [Tutorial about Due: None] \n\n6.5.3 Programming USB Port\nThis port allows the board to be programmed and powered via a USB connection to a computer. It facilitates serial communication between the Arduino Due and the computer, enabling the uploading of sketches and interaction with the Arduino IDE. The port is connected to the ATmega16U2 microcontroller, which acts as a USB-to-serial converter, simplifying the programming process. When connected to a computer, the Arduino IDE recognizes the board as a COM port, enabling seamless communication for programming and debugging purposes.",
      "product_category": "Mega",
      "chunk_id": "Due-datasheet::c32"
    },
    {
      "product": "Make Your UNO Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Make Your UNO Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Make Your UNO Kit: None] [Tutorial about Make Your UNO Kit: None] \n\nFeatures\nATMega328P Processor, Make Your UNOboard.Details = Memory. ATMega328P Processor, Make Your UNOboard.Details = AVR CPU at up to 16 MHz 32 kB Flash 2 kB SRAM 1 kB EEPROM. ATMega328P Processor, Make Your UNOboard.Details = Security. ATMega328P Processor, Make Your UNOboard.Details = Power On Reset (POR) Brown Out Detection (BOD). ATMega328P Processor, Make Your UNOboard.Details = Peripherals. ATMega328P Processor, Make Your UNOboard.Details = 2x 8-bit Timer/Counter with a dedicated period register and compare channels 1x 16-bit Timer/Counter with a dedicated period register, input capture and compare channels 1x USART with fractional baud rate generator and start-of-frame detection 1x controller/peripheral Serial Peripheral Interface (SPI) 1x Dual mode controller/peripheral I2C 1x Analog Comparator (AC) with a scalable reference input Watchdog Timer with separate on-chip oscillator 6x PWMchannels Interrupt and wake-up on pin change. USB-C® Serial PCB Board, Make Your UNOboard.Details = The USB-C® Serial PCB contains the ATMega16U2 processor and a USB-C® socket to program and power the board.. USB-C® Serial PCB Board, Make Your UNOboard.Details = The USB-C® Serial PCB contains the ATMega16U2 processor and a USB-C® socket to program and power the board.. USB-C® Serial PCB Board, Make Your UNOboard.Details = ATMega16U2 Processor. USB-C® Serial PCB Board, Make Your UNOboard.Details = 8-bit AVR® RISC-based microcontroller. USB-C® Serial PCB Board, Make Your UNOboard.Details = Memory. USB-C® Serial PCB Board, Make Your UNOboard.Details = 16 KB ISP Flash 512B EEPROM 512B SRAM debugWIRE interface for on-chip debugging and programming. USB-C® Serial PCB Board, Make Your UNOboard.Details = Power. USB-C® Serial PCB Board, Make Your UNOboard.Details = 2.7V-5.5V\nAudio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = Potentiometers. Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = 5x 10kΩ - Trimmer potentiometer - User programmable 1x 10kΩ - Trimmer potentiometer - Directly connected to the audio amplifier. Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = 5x 10kΩ - Trimmer potentiometer - User programmable 1x 10kΩ - Trimmer potentiometer - Directly connected to the audio amplifier. Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = Audio. Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = Amplifier: LM386. Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = Class-AB 4Ω Load 0.325W. Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = . Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = Speaker: L50EJ. Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = Impedance @2kHz: 8Ω Max Power 0.5W Output: 81dB +-3dB Diameter 45mm Weight: 48g. Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = . Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = . Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = . Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = . Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details = . Audio Synth Shield, Audio Synth Shield.Details =",
      "product_category": "Kits",
