      "product": "Modulino Distance",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Modulino Distance] [Product category: Modulino Family] [Element of Modulino Distance: None] [Tutorial about Modulino Distance: None] \n\n7 Functional Overview\nThe Modulino® Distance node uses a time-of-flight measuring principle to detect objects from 0 to ~1200 mm. It communicates via I2C (through the Qwiic connector at 3.3 V). GPIO1 can signal an interrupt when a threshold is reached or measurement is ready, while XSHUT can place the sensor in shutdown mode to save power.",
      "product_category": "Modulino Family",
      "chunk_id": "Modulino Distance-datasheet::c11"
    },
    {
      "product": "Nicla Vision",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Nicla Vision] [Product category: Nicla Family] [Element of Nicla Vision: None] [Tutorial about Nicla Vision: Tutorial_Nicla Vision] \n\n—— Click on the \"Play\" button at the bottom of the left toolbar. Place some objects on your desk and check if the Nicla Vision can detect them. The MicroPython script does not get compiled and linked into an actual firmware. e Instead it gets copied to the internal Flash of the board where it gets interpreted and executed on the fly. Conclusion In this tritarial voit laarned haw ta MicroPython scripts that then run on the Nicla Vision. You also learned how to configure the camera of the Nicla Vision to be used for machine vision applications in OpenMV. Last but not least you learned how to interact with the built-in LEDs in MicroPython on the OpenMV firmware. Next Steps Familiarize yourself with the OpenMV IDE. There are many other features that did not get mentioned in this tutorial (e.g. the Serial Terminal). Try out other machine vision examples",
      "product_category": "Nicla Family",
      "chunk_id": "Tutorial_Nicla Vision_Blob Detection with OpenMV::c15"
    },
    {
      "product": "Nicla Vision",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Nicla Vision] [Product category: Nicla Family] [Element of Nicla Vision: None] [Tutorial about Nicla Vision: None] \n\nDescription\nThe Arduino® Nicla Vision packs machine vision capabilities on the edge into a tiny fingerprint. Record, analyze and upload to the Cloud with the help of one Arduino® Nicla Vision . Leverage the onboard camera, STM32 microcontroller, Wi-Fi®/Bluetooth® module and 6-axis IMU to create your wireless sensor network for machine vision applications.",
      "product_category": "Nicla Family",
      "chunk_id": "Nicla Vision-datasheet::c0"
    },
