      "text": "[Product: Alvik] [Product category: Education] [Element of Alvik: None] [Tutorial about Alvik: Tutorial_Alvik] \n\nparameter inside the rectangle area, for example the number 5 or the cancel W_ element in the dropdown menu can be edited, to give Alvik a different behavior. ©© when button cancel ¥ is pressed ©O set left ¥ LEDcolorto YELLOW ¥ for @® seconds yellow LED rectangle commands Some blocks, for example in the Control section, have a hexagonal tile @ parameter, where you can drag and drop in an entire block, allowing you to nest commanas like for a Nesting parameters inside a block Blink Example Alvik comes with two built-in RGB LEDs, located on top of the robot. Alvik LEDs On the top of Alvik you can also find 8 buttons, that let you operate the robot. Alvik buttons The goal of our first program is to make the LEDs flash when you press a button on Alvik: 1 Navigate tothe Events folder and drag the command When button [ok] is pressed to the coding area on the right.",
