      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n2.3 Microcontroller\nProduct Name, Description = Arduino® UNO R4 WiFi. Microcontroller, Description = Renesas RA4M1 (R7FA4M1AB3CFM#AA0). Clock Speed, Description = 48 MHz. Power Supply, Description = 6-24 VDC via VIN, 5 VDC via USB-C®. Operating Voltage, Description = 5 V (RA4M1). Memory, Description = 256 kB Flash, 32 kB SRAM, 8 kB EEPROM. Peripherals, Description = Capacitive Touch Sensing Unit (CTSU), USB® 2.0 Full-Speed Module, 14-bit ADC, Up to DAC, Operational Amplifier (OPAMP). Communication, Description = 1x UART, 1x SPI, 1x I2C, 1x CAN (external transceiver required). Wi-Fi®, Description = 802.11 b/g/n (Wi-Fi® 4), up to 150 Mbps. Bluetooth®, Description = Bluetooth® 5. LED Matrix, Description = 12x8 red LEDs, fully programmable. Additional Features, Description = Real-time Clock (RTC), Memory Protection Unit (MPU), DAC, DMA. Certifications, Description = CE/RED, UKCA, FCC, IC, RoHS, REACH, WEEE",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c7"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n8.8 Modulino® Pixels\nThe Modulino® Pixels includes eight LC8822-2020 RGB LEDs and uses the STM32C011F4 chip for digital communication, perfect for creating colorful displays and lighting effects in your projects. All of the Modulino® nodes that use dedicated I2C interface controllers have the footprints to provide the option to mount I2C pullup resistors, but no resistors are mounted.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c52"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n1x10 Header for LC8822-2020 and I2C interface controller\nCO, Function = Clock Out. DO, Function = Data Out. RX1, Function = UART Receive. TX1, Function = UART Transmit. SWDIO, Function = SWD Data. SWCLK, Function = SWD Clock. PF2, Function = NRST\nThe header can be used to add more LC8822-2020 RGB's LED in a daisy chain configuration.\nBuilt-in LEDs open for extension\nIt also has other I2C interface controller IC pins usable for other purposes or for reprogramming it using its SWD interface. These provide a place to mount header pins if desired.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c56"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n8.9 Modulino® Buttons\nThe Modulino® Buttons includes three SPST push buttons and three yellow LEDs, using the STM32C011F4 chip for digital communication. It's ideal for creating interactive input interfaces. All of the Modulino® nodes that use dedicated I2C interface controllers have the footprints to provide the option to mount I2C pullup resistors, but no resistors are mounted.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c58"
    }
  ]
}", "source": "community:38", "id": "38", "score": ""}, {"content": "{
