    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\nDescription\nThe Arduino® Plug and Make Kit features the Arduino® UNO R4 WiFi with built-in Wi-Fi® capabilities, enabling connectivity and opening the doors to integration with the Arduino® Cloud platform. This kit includes a selection of seven Modulino® nodes, all easily connectable via I2C Qwiic cables. Tailor your project to perfection by selecting the sensors and inputs that best suit your needs, and experience a completely solder-free way to easily build your ideas. Dive into the world of electronics with hands-on learning and intuitive module interaction, empowering you to innovate and create with unparalleled ease and flexibility.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c0"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n2 Features\nThe Plug and Make Kit offers an intuitive and effortless introduction to the world of IoT and electronics. Featuring the powerful Arduino® UNO R4 WiFi, this kit enables seamless integration with the Arduino® Cloud for a smooth, wireless experience. With its array of modular sensors and components connectable via I2C Qwiic cables, the kit allows for easy customization of your projects. Equipped with a diverse range of sensors and interactive Modulino® nodes, this kit provides the tools you need to create dynamic and engaging projects with ease. Perfect for both beginners and experienced makers.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c4"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n2.1 Kit Content\nABX00080, Name = Arduino® UNO R4 WiFi. ABX00080, Purpose = Programmable main board. ABX00080, Quantity = 1. ASX00071, Name = Modulino® Base. ASX00071, Purpose = Base plate for UNO and Modulino® nodes. ASX00071, Quantity = 1. ABX00101, Name = Modulino® Movement. ABX00101, Purpose = Measure acceleration and rotation. ABX00101, Quantity = 1. ABX00102, Name = Modulino® Distance. ABX00102, Purpose = Time of flight, finds distances. ABX00102, Quantity = 1. ABX00103, Name = Modulino® Thermo. ABX00103, Purpose = Measure temperature and humidity. ABX00103, Quantity = 1. ABX00107, Name = Modulino® Knob. ABX00107, Purpose = Rotary encoder for input. ABX00107, Quantity = 1. ABX00108, Name = Modulino® Buzzer. ABX00108, Purpose = Produce sound. ABX00108, Quantity = 1. ABX00109, Name = Modulino® Pixels. ABX00109, Purpose = 8x RGB LEDs for display. ABX00109, Quantity = 1. ABX00110, Name = Modulino® Buttons. ABX00110, Purpose = 3x push buttons for input. ABX00110, Quantity = 1",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c5"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n7 Modulino® Base\nThe Modulino® Base is designed to provide a stable and secure mounting solution for your Arduino® UNO R4 WiFi and additional nodes. Measuring 140x140x1.6 mm with 3.5 mm holes, it ensures that your setup remains firm and organized, making it easier to manage your components and connections.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c16"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n5 Block Diagram\nThe Plug and Make Kit is a combination of the Arduino UNO R4 Wifi board connected to different Modulino® nodes boards through and I2C bus as can be seen in the following block diagram.\nPlug and Make Kit block diagram",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c10"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n8.1.3 I2C Address Reference\nEach Modulino® node of the kit is designed to be connected to the Arduino® UNO R4 WiFi microcontroller using the Qwiic connectors available on both sides of the Modulino® nodes. The first node is connected to the microcontroller while the rest are connected to the latest one creating a physical \"daisy-chain\" connection that, from the communication point of view, is an I2C bus line where all the devices are connected acting the Arduino® UNO R4 WiFi as the controller and the Modulino® nodes as the targets.\nIn the case multiple nodes of the same kind are connected to the I2C \"daisy-chain\", they may have the same I2C default address, causing communication problems. All Modulino® nodes are designed to have the possibility of having different I2C addresses via hardware or firmware changes as presented in the following table.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c22"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n8.1.3 I2C Address Reference\nMODULINO MOVEMENT, Sensor/Actuator = LSM6DSOXTR. MODULINO MOVEMENT, Modulino® I2C Address (HEX) = 0x6A. MODULINO MOVEMENT, Editable Addresses (HEX) = 0x6A, 0x6B (via solder jumper). MODULINO MOVEMENT, Hardware I2C Address (HEX) = 0x6A & 0x7E. MODULINO DISTANCE, Sensor/Actuator = VL53L4CDV0DH/1. MODULINO DISTANCE, Modulino® I2C Address (HEX) = 0x29. MODULINO DISTANCE, Editable Addresses (HEX) = Any custom address (via software configuration). MODULINO DISTANCE, Hardware I2C Address (HEX) = 0x29. MODULINO THERMO, Sensor/Actuator = HS3003. MODULINO THERMO, Modulino® I2C Address (HEX) = 0x44. MODULINO THERMO, Editable Addresses (HEX) = Any custom address (via software configuration). MODULINO THERMO, Hardware I2C Address (HEX) = 0x44. MODULINO BUZZER, Sensor/Actuator = PKLCS1212E4001. MODULINO BUZZER, Modulino® I2C Address (HEX) = 0x3C. MODULINO BUZZER, Editable Addresses (HEX) = Any custom address (via software configuration). MODULINO BUZZER, Hardware I2C Address (HEX) = 0x1E. MODULINO KNOB, Sensor/Actuator = PEC11J-9215F-S0015. MODULINO KNOB, Modulino® I2C Address (HEX) = 0x76. MODULINO KNOB, Editable Addresses (HEX) = Any custom address (via software configuration). MODULINO KNOB, Hardware I2C Address (HEX) = 0x3A. MODULINO PIXELS, Sensor/Actuator = Eight LC8822-2020. MODULINO PIXELS, Modulino® I2C Address (HEX) = 0x6C. MODULINO PIXELS, Editable Addresses (HEX) = Any custom address (via software configuration). MODULINO PIXELS, Hardware I2C Address (HEX) = 0x36. MODULINO BUTTONS, Sensor/Actuator = Three SPST Push Buttons. MODULINO BUTTONS, Modulino® I2C Address (HEX) = 0x7C. MODULINO BUTTONS, Editable Addresses (HEX) = Any custom address (via software configuration). MODULINO BUTTONS, Hardware I2C Address (HEX) = 0x3E\nPlease note: When scanning for I2C addresses connected to the bus, the boards might identify themselves using the Hardware I2C Address listed in the last column of the table. However, you should always use the Modulino® I2C Address provided in your code if using the official Modulino® library.\nWith the provided software, users can change the default I2C address of the dedicated I2C interface controller firmware. Assigning different addresses allows users to connect multiple boards of the same type in a chain. To facilitate this, a white rectangle is positioned on the bottom silk of the board, where users can write the new I2C address directly on the board itself.\nBlank silk for identification",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c23"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n1x4 Header\nGND, Function = Ground. 3.3 V, Function = Power Supply. SDA, Function = I2C Data. SCL, Function = I2C Clock\nThe above pads are generic to all Modulino® nodes and they are on the same bus as the Qwiic connectors. These provide a place to mount header pins if desired.\nModulino® Thermo Pinout\nModulino Thermo SKU code:ABX00103 Pinout Last update: 18 Jun, 2024",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c41"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n8.4 Modulino® Distance\nThe Modulino® Distance, featuring the VL53L4CDV0DH/1 sensor, provides accurate distance measurements using time-of-flight technology. It's perfect for applications requiring precise distance sensing, such as robotics and proximity sensors.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c33"
    },
    {
      "product": "Plug and Make Kit",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Plug and Make Kit] [Product category: Kits] [Element of Plug and Make Kit: None] [Tutorial about Plug and Make Kit: None] \n\n8.6 Modulino® Knob\nThe Modulino® Knob includes a quadrature rotary encoder with an SPST switch, using the STM32C011F4 chip for digital communication. This setup allows precise control for user interfaces and adjustments in various applications. All of the Modulino® nodes that use dedicated I2C interface controllers have the footprints to provide the option to mount I2C pullup resistors, but no resistors are mounted.",
      "product_category": "Kits",
      "chunk_id": "Plug and Make Kit-datasheet::c42"
    }
  ]
}", "source": "community:60", "id": "60", "score": ""}, {"content": "{
