    },
    {
      "product": "Nano Matter",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Nano Matter] [Product category: Nano Family] [Element of Nano Matter: None] [Tutorial about Nano Matter: Tutorial_Nano Matter] \n\nHardware and Software Requirements Hardware Requirements Arduino Nano Matter (x1) Grove motor driver module (x1) DC motor (x1) Breadboard (x1) Jumper wires Google Nest Hub Max (Thread Border Router) (x1) USB-C® cable (x1) Software Requirements Arduino IDE 2.0+ or Arduino Cloud Editor Google Home App Download the Project Code DOWNLOAD THE CODE y Download the complete project code here. Board Core and Libraries The Silicon Labs core contains the libraries and examples you need to work with the board's components, such as its Matter, Bluetooth® Low Energy, and I/Os. To install the Nano Matter core, navigate to Tools > Board > Boards Manager or click the Boards Manager icon in the left tab of the IDE. In the Boards Manager tab, search for Nano Matter and install the latest Silicon Labs core version.",
      "product_category": "Nano Family",
      "chunk_id": "Tutorial_Nano Matter_Smart Fan::c2"
    },
    {
      "product": "Nano Matter",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Nano Matter] [Product category: Nano Family] [Element of Nano Matter: None] [Tutorial about Nano Matter: Tutorial_Nano Matter] \n\nOnce you uploaded the example code to the Nano Matter, open the Serial Monitor and reset the board. QR Code URL After the reset you will find on the serial port the URL that generates the QR for the Matter device commissioning. Adding the Device (Commissioning) Copy and paste the QR code URL on your favorite web browser and a unique QR code will be generated for your board. Go to your Google Home app, navigate to devices and tap on Add, select the Matter-enabled device option and scan the QR code. TY Adding the device to Google Home app Your device is successfully added Final Results Finally, you will be able to control the fan from your smartphone, hub or asking your personal assistant. Conclusion In this tutorial we have learned how to create a Matter enabled fan that can be controlled from our smartphone and personal assistant. The Nano Matter allows us to seamlessly integrate our own custom or old fan as a commercial product with our current smart home ecosystem.",
      "product_category": "Nano Family",
      "chunk_id": "Tutorial_Nano Matter_Smart Fan::c6"
    },
    {
      "product": "Nano Matter",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Nano Matter] [Product category: Nano Family] [Element of Nano Matter: None] [Tutorial about Nano Matter: Tutorial_Nano Matter] \n\ngit clone --recurse-submo Install prerequisites:\nBefore building, you must install a few OS specific dependencies. ( >) sudo apt-get install git gq libglib2.@-dev libavg python3-pip unzip lib default-jre SY Open a command prompt in the connectedhomeip directory and run the following command:\ncd connectedhomeip scripts/examples/gn_build CHIP Tool environment set Wait for the packages installation process to finish. To check if the CHIP Tool runs correctly, execute the following command:",
      "product_category": "Nano Family",
      "chunk_id": "Tutorial_Nano Matter_Border Router ESP32::c8"
    },
    {
      "product": "Nano Matter",
      "file": "docling_chunks.jsonl",
      "text": "[Product: Nano Matter] [Product category: Nano Family] [Element of Nano Matter: None] [Tutorial about Nano Matter: Tutorial_Nano Matter] \n\nThis allows the Nano Matter to be integrated with smart home systems and communicate wirelessly with other devices. Pinout Nano Matter Simple pinout The full pinout is available and downloadable as PDF from the link below:",
      "product_category": "Nano Family",
      "chunk_id": "Tutorial_Nano Matter_User Manual::c4"
    }
  ]
